WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.350
Count the hairdressers across a
country and you reach the thousands.

2
00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:07.120
Now try to buy a large passenger jet.

3
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.070
Two firms make most of them.

4
00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:14.450
In 2023, Airbus delivered
735 commercial aircraft,

5
00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:17.360
and Boeing delivered 528.

6
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.770
So why do some industries
have thousands of small firms,

7
00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:23.130
while others have only two or three?

8
00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.960
In this mission, you'll
build a firm's long-run cost

9
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.640
curve out of many short-run curves.

10
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.890
Then you'll find the output where
long-run average cost stops falling,

11
00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:35.060
and see why that point matters.

12
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:38.920
Your mission: explain why some
industries hold many firms

13
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.360
and others just a few.
